From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: emuTOS-MCD <darekadumon@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 19:24:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 151/184] Boot never touches the disc, and a silent drive
 cannot eat the clock

"It shouldn't take as long to boot, and the failure takes forever."
Both traced, both bounded.

Boot: segacd_cd_rw() now refuses instantly while cd_booting. The boot
probe's reads have never once succeeded on this hardware, and each one
was expensive -- a leash that cannot expire when the drive is not
reporting, since cd_time_left() counts cdd_ticks and cdd_ticks is
frozen exactly then, plus disk_init_one's retries, plus the dead-drive
latch as a parting gift (which is why the first click's dialog was
instant while the boot crawled). D: keeps its drive letter: the unit is
removable, so disk_init_one assigns a BGM partition without a
successful read -- every dump with drvbits 0000000F is that path.

The forever: cd_prepare()'s settle wait was outside every budget. Six
rounds of 200,000 spins, inside up to eight attempts, and its
cd_time_left() bound is the same frozen clock. Minutes of spinning per
fill on a drive that is not answering. It now pays from cd_budget, the
fill-wide spin backstop that exists for exactly this case, and gives up
when the budget is gone.

What remains long, once, and deliberately: the first D: access after
the desktop still runs the firmware wake, and if that fails it costs
its DRV_INIT budget before the dialog appears. It fires once per
session -- cd_ts_decided latches -- so every click after the first
fails in seconds, not tens.

Not verified in the emulator: the click itself. I could not script a
reliable double-click on the DISK D icon, so the emulator run proves
booting is clean, the desktop is up, no read fires at boot, and nothing
regressed -- not that the icon opens. The remount-offer chain it relies
on is the one the v19 hardware run demonstrably entered (the rescans
were the slow part), so the path is live; whether it now succeeds is a
hardware question.
---
 bios/scdapi.h |  2 +-
 bios/segacd.c | 34 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 2 files changed, 33 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/bios/scdapi.h b/bios/scdapi.h
index bb5101a..7534f06 100644
--- a/bios/scdapi.h
+++ b/bios/scdapi.h
@@ -28,7 +28,7 @@
 #define SCDAPI_H
 
 #define SCD_COOKIE   0x53674344L        /* 'SgCD' */
-#define SCD_VERSION  19
+#define SCD_VERSION  20
 
 /* Everything the disc diagnostic prints, in one go. Taken in a single
  * call rather than twenty accessors so that the numbers in one report
diff --git a/bios/segacd.c b/bios/segacd.c
index fa82a97..54c51b5 100644
--- a/bios/segacd.c
+++ b/bios/segacd.c
@@ -2234,9 +2234,20 @@ static UBYTE cd_prepare(void)
             UBYTE base = cdd_irqs;
             LONG spin = 200000L;
 
-            while (spin-- > 0 && (UBYTE)(cdd_irqs - base) < 12)
-                ;
+            /* Also bounded by the fill's own backstop. This wait was
+             * outside every budget: six rounds of 200,000 spins, inside
+             * up to eight attempts, and cd_time_left() cannot expire
+             * while the drive is not reporting because cdd_ticks is
+             * frozen exactly then. That is minutes of spinning, per
+             * fill, on a silent drive -- "it takes forever just to
+             * fail" was mostly this loop. cd_budget exists for
+             * precisely this case; make the loop pay from it. */
+            while (spin-- > 0 && cd_budget > 0
+                   && (UBYTE)(cdd_irqs - base) < 12)
+                cd_budget--;
         }
+        if (cd_budget <= 0)
+            break;
     }
     return CD_NOTREADY;
 }
@@ -3268,6 +3279,25 @@ LONG segacd_cd_rw(WORD rw, LONG sector, WORD count, UBYTE *buf)
 {
     if (rw & RW_WRITE)
         return EWRPRO;
+    /* Refuse everything until the desktop is up. Instantly, before any
+     * counter moves.
+     *
+     * The boot probe's reads have never once succeeded on this
+     * hardware and each one is expensive: a leash that cannot expire
+     * when the drive is not reporting (cd_time_left counts cdd_ticks,
+     * and cdd_ticks is frozen exactly then), retries on top, and then
+     * the dead-drive latch as a parting gift -- which is what made the
+     * first click's error dialog appear "immediately" while the boot
+     * itself crawled. All cost, no sector, every boot.
+     *
+     * D: still gets its drive letter -- the unit is removable, so
+     * disk_init_one() assigns a BGM partition whether or not the probe
+     * read anything; every dump with drvbits 0000000F proves that path.
+     * The volume is simply not logged yet, and the media-change offer
+     * re-runs Getbpb on the first touch after the desktop, under the
+     * only conditions a read has ever worked here. */
+    if (cd_booting)
+        return EREADF;
     if (sector < 0 || (ULONG)sector + count > CD_DDISK_BLOCKS)
         return ESECNF;
     if (cd_dead) {
